# Shared edge proxy for every Roomie Status cluster on the VPS.
#
# This is the only Caddy on the box bound to the host's 80/443. It terminates
# TLS (Let's Encrypt, HTTP-01 on port 80) for both public hostnames and forwards
# each one to the matching app cluster's Caddy over the external `roomie-edge`
# network, addressing it by the alias docker/docker-compose.deploy.yml registers
# (`roomie-<env>-frontend`).
#
# The hostnames come from the environment (set by the deploy workflow from the
# DEV_SITE_DOMAIN / MAIN_SITE_DOMAIN repository variables) so no domain is
# hard-coded here. Upstream names are resolved per request, not at startup, so
# the edge comes up and keeps serving one site while the other cluster is down,
# mid-redeploy, or not created yet — a dev deploy can never take prod offline.
#
# Compression is left to the cluster's own Caddy: the client's Accept-Encoding
# is forwarded as-is, so responses are compressed once, at the origin.

{$DEV_SITE_DOMAIN} {
	reverse_proxy roomie-dev-frontend:80
}

{$MAIN_SITE_DOMAIN} {
	reverse_proxy roomie-prod-frontend:80
}
